  "name": "Pokémon Card Game Official Visual Book",
  "category": "publication_promotion",
  "description": {
    "text": "Media Factory's Official Visual Books of the Diamond & Pearl era showed every card of the latest expansions and starter products, sorted by type by the Pokémon Card Laboratory, with sample decks and the rules. Each came with a holo card drawn only for it, and the DP books also with a poster. The five DP books' cards were all LV.X Pokémon: Lucario LV.X 004/DP-P with the first, in December 2006, Garchomp LV.X with the Secret of the Lakes and Shining Darkness edition in July 2007, Porygon-Z LV.X with the Moonlit Pursuit and Dawn Dash edition, Heatran LV.X with the Cry from the Mysterious and Temple of Anger edition in March 2008, and Drapion LV.X with the Intense Fight in the Destroyed Sky edition in August 2008. Ryo Ueda drew all of them but Heatran, which Shizurow drew. The first DPt book, the Galactic's Conquest edition of October 2008, came with Ryota Saito's Toxicroak G, 008/DPt-P.",
